This folder holds the parts that must exist before Flux can work. Flux does
not manage them. You deploy changes here by hand. On main, the image tags
here are dummy values. A release branch has the real tags.

Deploy the parts together:

kubectl apply -k https://github.com/teapotovh/teapot//release/<tag>/release/base?ref=<tag>

New cluster? Run in this order:

kubectl apply -k https://github.com/teapotovh/teapot//release/<tag>/release/flux?ref=<tag>
kubectl apply -k bootstrap
kubectl apply -k https://github.com/teapotovh/teapot//release/<tag>/release/kustomizations?ref=<tag>

Fill in the secret files before you apply. tools/release prints these
commands after you push a tag.
